body:
partial on mkinney:issue/637-carried-stock-field · PR #1140 (draft, Refs) · step E3: the app holders (`stock_sim_carry`, `rest`, `rest/across`, `PriorPlan`) carry stock as `CarriedStock` on either engine, column engine still the default · pinned by sim `carried_stock` (6) and the heavy lane `carried_engine_agreement::both_engines_read_every_carried_document_alike` (release, `--ignored`: 14 documents of the `setup_carry` / `rest_across_setups` / `carried_verify` fixtures, 0 findings); the carried suites also pass whole on the field arm (`CAMCRAFT_CARRY_ENGINE=field`) · quick gate green on 68d317b7 · merges when reviewed.

Left after this PR (field arm only; nothing shipped depends on it):
- a cylinder stock is refused by name on the field arm (its mesh holds less than the round at the rim) - needs a round with the column disc's rim law;
- no lane document uses a from-model stock, or a ball / taper / bull-nose tool across a carry;
- a cut-through column reports the gouge to the stock's floor, not the tool's depth below it (same class as the column engine, smaller magnitude) - #589 should accept or change that before the default flips;
- the operation priors still take the read-back tops as a `Dexel` through `Columns::of_grid` (#586's remaining work), and the field arm is slow in debug.
